# INTEGER (0..18446744073709551615) against pycrate, asn1c and rasn: every
# check against pycrate passes, in both variants.
#
# asn1c cannot hold the range: its UNALIGNED encoder and decoder stop on
# an assertion (uper_support.c per__imax_range "Unreachable") and its
# ALIGNED decoder rejects every value. rasn decodes the counters but its
# JER printer stops at 2^63 - 1 ("Exceeds supported integer range"), and in
# ALIGNED it does not octet-align a fixed OCTET STRING over two octets
# (startTime, X.691 17.7), a deviation recorded for other modules too.
deviates asn1c Counter
deviates asn1c Report
deviates asn1c Reports
deviates rasn Counter
deviates rasn Report
deviates rasn Reports
